msgid "Ranking: Mexican State Flags and Auto-Team Registration"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"This fork ships two enhancements to the Ranking Web Server targeted at "
"the OMI:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Bundled flags** — real flag images for all 32 Mexican states, served "
"automatically by the ranking server."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Auto-team registration** — teams are created from the flag images found"
" in `lib_dir/flags/` every time the ranking server starts."
msgstr ""

msgid "How auto-team registration works"
msgstr ""

msgid "On startup, `cmsRankingWebServer` calls `seed_flags_and_teams`, which:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Copies the 32 bundled state flag PNG files into `lib_dir/flags/` "
"(default: `.venv/lib/ranking/flags/`), overwriting any existing copies of"
" those bundled files."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Scans `lib_dir/flags/` for image files (`.png`, `.jpg`, `.gif`, `.bmp`) "
"and creates a **team** entry for each filename stem not yet registered."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The team name is resolved from the filename stem: if it matches a known "
"Mexican state code (e.g. `JAL`) the full state name is used (`Jalisco`); "
"otherwise the stem itself becomes the team name."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Teams are only *created*, never automatically updated or deleted. Once a "
"team exists it can be renamed or modified through the admin interface "
"without losing changes on the next restart."
msgstr ""

